1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,500
How big should your emergency fund be?

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:04,541
Count essentials, not income.

3
00:00:04,961 --> 00:00:12,247
In our example, rent, car, insurance, utilities, phone, minimums, groceries and gas come to $3,011 a month.

4
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:17,403
3 months is $9,033. Six months, about $18,000.

5
00:00:17,823 --> 00:00:21,039
Too big? Start with one month of bills, then build from there.

6
00:00:21,809 --> 00:00:23,616
How to pick your number is on my channel.
